#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:55
msgid "Changes to the LLVM IR"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:57
msgid ""
"Removed `llvm.convert.to.fp16` and `llvm.convert.from.fp16` intrinsics. "
"These are equivalent to `fptrunc` and `fpext` with half with a bitcast."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:61
msgid ""
"\"denormal-fp-math\" and \"denormal-fp-math-f32\" string attributes were "
"migrated to first-class denormal_fpenv attribute."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:64
msgid ""
"The `\"nooutline\"` attribute is now writen as `nooutline`. Existing IR and "
"bitcode will be automatically updated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:67
msgid ""
"`ConstantPointerNull` can now represent fixed and scalable vector splats of "
"null pointers. Such constants may print as `splat (ptr null)` instead of "
"`zeroinitializer`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:71
msgid "LLVM IR floating-point literals have greatly changed:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:73
msgid ""
"The old hexadecimal bitwise representation is deprecated and will be removed "
"in the next revision. It is replaced with a unified `f0x` prefix."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:76
msgid "Hexadecimal literals akin to C99's syntax are supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:78
msgid ""
"Special values for infinities and NaNs, including NaN payloads, are added."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:80
msgid ""
"The standard textual output for floating-point literals is changed to take "
"advantage of the new floating-point literals formats."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:83
msgid ""
"The resume/destroy functions emitted for the switch-resume ABI (C++20 "
"coroutines) now use `CallingConv::C` instead of `CallingConv::Fast`. This "
"stabilizes the coroutine ABI across LLVM versions and aligns it with other "
"vendors. The change is observationally identical on targets where `fastcc` "
"and `ccc` agree for `void(ptr)` (x86_64, AArch64, RISC-V, ...) but is an ABI "
"break on i686, MIPS O32, PowerPC64 ELFv1, and Lanai."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:90
msgid "Fast math flags are now permitted on `uitofp` and `sitofp`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:92
msgid "Changes to LLVM infrastructure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:94
msgid ""
"Removed ``Constant::isZeroValue``. It was functionally identical to "
"``Constant::isNullValue`` for all types except floating-point negative zero. "
"All callers should use ``isNullValue`` instead. ``isZeroValue`` will be "
"reintroduced in the future with bitwise-all-zeros semantics to support non-"
"zero null pointers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:100
msgid ""
"Added support for specifying the null pointer bit representation per address "
"space in `DataLayout`. Pointer specifications (`p`) accept new flags: `z` "
"(null is all-zeros) and `o` (null is all-ones). Address spaces without an "
"explicit flag default to all-zeros. See the `DataLayout` section of the "
"[LangRef](https://llvm.org/docs/LangRef.html#data-layout) for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:107
msgid "Removed TypePromoteFloat legalization from SelectionDAG"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:109
msgid ""
"Removed `bugpoint`. Usage has been replaced by `llvm-reduce` and `llvm/utils/"
"reduce_pipeline.py`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:112
msgid ""
"The ``Br`` opcode was split into two opcodes separating unconditional "
"(``UncondBr``) and conditional (``CondBr``) branches."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:115
msgid ""
"``BranchInst`` was deprecated in favor of ``UncondBrInst`` and "
"``CondBrInst``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:117
msgid ""
"The operand order of ``CondBr`` instructions was adjusted to match the "
"successor order. This can cause subtle breakage when using ``getOperand`` or "
"``setOperand`` to access successors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:121
msgid "The ``llvm::sys::fs`` link creation API has been refactored:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:123
msgid ""
"``create_link`` now tries to create a symbolic link first, falling back to a "
"hard link if that fails (previously it created a symlink on Unix and a hard "
"link on Windows)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:126
msgid ""
"Added ``create_symlink``, which always creates a symbolic link. On windows "
"this may fail if symlink permissions are not available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:128
msgid "Added ``readlink``, which reads the target of a symbolic link."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:130
msgid ""
"Bitcode libraries can now implement compiler-managed library functions "
"(libcalls) without causing incorrect API manipulation or undefined "
"references ([#177046](https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/pull/125687)). "
"Note that there are still issues with invalid compiler reasoning about some "
"functions in bitcode, e.g. `malloc`. Not yet supported on MachO or when "
"using distributed ThinLTO."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:137
msgid ""
"``ConstantFP`` now supports vector types and is the canonical form returned "
"by ``ConstantVector::getSplat(C)`` when ``C`` is a scalar ``ConstantFP``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:140
msgid ""
"``DenseMap`` and ``DenseSet`` ``erase`` now invalidates all iterators and "
"references into the container, not just the iterator for the erased element. "
"Use the new ``remove_if`` member to erase matching elements in a single pass "
"instead of erasing while iterating."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:145
msgid ""
"``TargetRegisterInfo::getMinimalPhysRegClass`` and related APIs have been "
"refactored and no longer take a type. This API is also now precomputed in "
"TableGen to improve compile-time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:149
msgid "Changes to building LLVM"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:151
msgid "Changes to TableGen"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:153
msgid ""
"Outer let statements use ``ID{n-m}`` instead of ``ID<n-m>`` to be consistent "
"with inner let statements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:156
msgid "Changes to Interprocedural Optimizations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:158
msgid "Changes to Vectorizers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:160
msgid "Changes to the AArch64 Backend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:162
msgid ""
"The `sysp`, `mrrs`, and `msrr` instructions are now accepted without "
"requiring the `+d128` feature gating."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:164
msgid ""
"Added a new internal option `-aarch64-emit-debug-tls-location` to allow the "
"emission of `DW_AT_location` for thread-local variables. This is currently "
"disabled by default to maintain compatibility with Binutils and LLVM older "
"toolchains that do not define the `R_AARCH64_TLS_DTPREL64` static relocation "
"type for TLS offsets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:169
msgid ""
"A bug was fixed that caused LLVM IR inline assembly clobbers of the x29 and "
"x30 registers to be ignored when they were written using their xN names "
"instead of the ABI names FP and LR. Note that LLVM IR produced by Clang "
"always uses the ABI names, but other frontends may not. ([#167783](https://"
"github.com/llvm/llvm-project/pull/167783))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:175
msgid "Changes to the AMDGPU Backend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:177
msgid "Initial support for gfx1310"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:178
msgid ""
"The `\"amdgpu-num-sgpr\"` and `\"amdgpu-num-vgpr\"` IR function attributes "
"(generated by the Clang `amdgpu_num_sgpr` and `amdgpu_num_vgpr` attributes) "
"are now deprecated. Use `\"amdgpu-waves-per-eu\"` instead. The backend still "
"honors the attributes; Clang emits a `-Wdeprecated-declarations` warning "
"when the source attributes are used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:183
msgid ""
"The `relaxed-buffer-oob-mode` subtarget feature has been replaced by two "
"module flags, `amdgpu.buffer.oob.mode` and `amdgpu.tbuffer.oob.mode`, which "
"control out-of-bounds semantics (see the AMDGPU User Guide). Frontends that "
"previously relied on the subtarget feature to enable misaligned buffer "
"merging must now set the corresponding module flag to `1` (relaxed). An "
"absent flag is treated as strict by the backend."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:190
msgid "Changes to the ARM Backend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:192
msgid ""
"The `r14` register can now be used as an alias for the link register `lr` in "
"inline assembly. Clang always canonicalizes the name to `lr`, but other "
"frontends may not."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:196
msgid "Changes to the AVR Backend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:198
msgid "Changes to the DirectX Backend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:200
msgid "Changes to the Hexagon Backend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:202
msgid "Changes to the LoongArch Backend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:204
msgid ""
"DWARF fission is now compatible with linker relaxations, allowing `-gsplit-"
"dwarf` and `-mrelax` to be used together when building for the LoongArch "
"platform."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:207
msgid "Changes to the MIPS Backend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:209
msgid "Changes to the NVPTX Backend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:211
msgid ""
"The default SM version has been changed from `sm_30` to `sm_75`. `sm_75` is "
"the oldest GPU variant compatible with the widest range of recent major CUDA "
"Toolkit versions (11/12/13)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:215
msgid "Changes to the PowerPC Backend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:217
msgid "Changes to the RISC-V Backend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:219
msgid "`llvm-objdump` now has support for `--symbolize-operands` with RISC-V."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:220
msgid "`-mcpu=spacemit-x100` was added."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:221
msgid "Change P extension version to match the 0.21 draft specification."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:222
msgid ""
"Mnemonics for MOP/HINT-based instructions (`lpad`, `pause`, `ntl.*`, `c.ntl."
"*`, `sspush`, `sspopchk`, `ssrdp`, `c.sspush`, `c.sspopchk`) are now always "
"available in the assembler and disassembler without requiring their "
"respective extensions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:226
msgid ""
"Adds experimental assembler support for the 'Zvabd` (RISC-V Integer Vector "
"Absolute Difference) extension."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:228
msgid "Adds CodeGen support for the 'Zvabd` extension."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:229
msgid "`-mcpu=spacemit-a100` was added."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:230
msgid ""
"The opt-in `-riscv-enable-p-ext-simd-codegen` flag has been removed. P "
"extension SIMD code generation is now enabled automatically if the P "
"extension is supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:231
msgid "`-mcpu=xt-c910v2` and `-mcpu=xt-c920v2` were added."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:232
msgid ""
"Adds experimental assembler support for the 'Zvzip` (RISC-V Vector "
"Reordering Structured Data) extension."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:234
msgid "`-mcpu=sifive-x160` and `-mcpu=sifive-x180` were added."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:235
msgid ""
"Support for the experimental `XRivosVisni` vendor extension has been removed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:236
msgid ""
"Support for the experimental `XRivosVizip` vendor extension has been removed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:237
msgid ""
"Adds experimental assembler support for the 'Zvvmm` (RISC-V Integer Matrix "
"Multiply-Accumulate) extension."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:238
msgid ""
"Adds experimental assembler support for the 'Zvvfmm` (RISC-V Floating-Point "
"Matrix Multiply-Accumulate) extension."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:239
msgid ""
"Adds experimental assembler support for the 'Zvvmtls` and 'Zvvmttls` (RISC-V "
"Matrix Tile Load/Store) extensions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:241
msgid ""
"Adds support for 'Ziccid' (Instruction/Data Coherence and Consistency) "
"extension."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:242
msgid ""
"Adds experimental assembler support for the `Xqccmt` (Qualcomm 16-bit Table "
"Jump) vendor extension."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:243
msgid "`-mcpu=sifive-870` has been renamed `-mcpu=sifive-p870-d`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:244
msgid ""
"Adds experimental assembler support for batched dot-product "
"extensions(Zvqwbdota8i, Zvqwbdota16i, Zvfwbdota16bf, Zvfqwbdota8f and "
"Zvfbdota32f)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:245
msgid ""
"Adds experimental assembler support for dot-product extensions(Zvqwdota8i, "
"Zvqwdota16i, Zvfwdota16bf and Zvfqwdota8f)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:247
msgid "Changes to the WebAssembly Backend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:249
msgid "Changes to the Windows Target"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:251
msgid ""
"The `.seh_startchained` and `.seh_endchained` assembly instructions have "
"been removed and replaced with a new `.seh_splitchained` instruction."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:254
msgid "Changes to the X86 Backend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:256
msgid ""
"`.att_syntax` directive is now emitted for assembly files when AT&T syntax "
"is in use. This matches the behaviour of Intel syntax and aids with "
"compatibility when changing the default Clang syntax to the Intel syntax."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:260
msgid ""
"Implemented Win64 APX ABI callee-saved registers: R30 and R31 are now "
"treated as non-volatile in the Win64 calling convention when APX is "
"available, per the Microsoft x64 calling convention specification."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:264
msgid ""
"Functions using setjmp with Win64 APX ABI now reserve R30/R31 from register "
"allocation, as the unwinder cannot restore APX extended registers across "
"longjmp. A warning is emitted for large functions where this reservation may "
"impact performance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:269
msgid "Changes to the OCaml bindings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:271
msgid "Changes to the Python bindings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:273
msgid "Changes to the C API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:275
msgid "Replaced opcode ``LLVMBr`` with ``LLVMUncondBr`` and ``LLVMCondBr``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:277
msgid ""
"The operand order of ``CondBr`` instructions was adjusted to match the "
"successor order. This can cause subtle breakage when using "
"``LLVMGetOperand`` or ``LLVMSetOperand`` to access successors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:281
msgid "Changes to the CodeGen infrastructure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:283
msgid ""
"Renamed ISD::CTLZ_ZERO_UNDEF to ISD::CTLZ_ZERO_POISON opcode to make it "
"clear that a zero input results in poison."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:286
msgid ""
"Renamed ISD::CTTZ_ZERO_UNDEF to ISD::CTTZ_ZERO_POISON opcode to make it "
"clear that a zero input results in poison."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:289
msgid "Changes to the GlobalISel infrastructure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:291
msgid ""
"Renamed G_CTLZ_ZERO_UNDEF to G_CTLZ_ZERO_POISON opcode to make it clear that "
"a zero input results in poison."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:294
msgid ""
"Renamed G_CTTZ_ZERO_UNDEF to G_CTTZ_ZERO_POISON opcode to make it clear that "
"a zero input results in poison."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:297
msgid ""
"GlobalISel's IRTranslator now supports the LLVM IR byte type (`bN`). Byte "
"values are translated as the equi-sized integer scalar (`sN`), "
"`ConstantByte` is materialised via `G_CONSTANT`, and `bitcast` between a "
"byte type and a pointer is lowered to `G_INTTOPTR` / `G_PTRTOINT` rather "
"than the verifier-illegal `G_BITCAST`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:303
msgid "Changes to the Metadata Info"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:305
msgid "Changes to the Debug Info"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:307
msgid "Changes to the LLVM tools"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:309
msgid ""
"`llvm-profgen` now supports ETM trace decoding using the OpenCSD library for "
"Cortex-M targets. OpenCSD version 1.5.4 or higher is required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:311
msgid ""
"`llvm-objcopy` no longer corrupts the symbol table when `--update-section` "
"is called for ELF files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:312
msgid ""
"`FileCheck` option `-check-prefix` now accepts a comma-separated list of "
"prefixes, making it an alias of the existing `-check-prefixes` option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:314
msgid "Add `-mtune` option to `llc`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:315
msgid "Add `-mtune` option to `opt`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:316
msgid ""
"Fixed `llvm-ar` to correctly handle the `N` count modifier on Windows for "
"archive members whose names differ only in case (e.g. `FOO.OBJ` and `foo."
"obj`). Previously, `-N 2` would fail with \"not found\" even when two "
"matching members existed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:319
msgid "Changes to LLDB"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:321
msgid ""
"A new ``webinspector-wasm`` platform was added to list and attach to "
"WebAssembly processes in Safari."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:322
msgid ""
"The default for `load-script-from-symbol-file` was changed from `warn` to "
"`trusted`. This means that scripts from code signed dSYM bundles are now "
"loaded automatically, while untrusted bundles continue to produce a warning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:324
msgid ""
"Pressing enter after `frame variable` repeats the command with an "
"incremented `--depth` option, allowing quick expansion of nested data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:326
msgid ""
"Breakpoint commands now accept `.` to refer to the location(s) at which the "
"current thread is stopped. For example, `breakpoint disable .` disables the "
"just-hit breakpoint location. Another usage is to automate a command to run "
"at the current location: `breakpoint command add -o 'p my_var' .`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:329
msgid "The `apropos` command now:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:330
msgid "Highlights matching keywords in its output when color is enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:331
msgid ""
"Searches the components of settings paths. For example `apropos qemu-user` "
"will now show `platform.plugin.qemu-user` as one of the results."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:334
msgid "Deprecated APIs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:336
msgid ""
"``SBTarget::GetDataByteSize()``, ``SBTarget::GetCodeByteSize()``, and "
"``SBSection::GetTargetByteSize()`` have been deprecated. They always return "
"`1`, as before."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:339
msgid "FreeBSD"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:341
msgid "Userspace Debugging"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:343
msgid "Support for MIPS64 has been removed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:344
msgid ""
"The minimum assumed FreeBSD version is now 14. The effect of which is that "
"watchpoints are assumed to be supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:347
msgid "Kernel Debugging"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:349
msgid ""
"The plugin that analyzes FreeBSD kernel core dump and live core has been "
"renamed from `freebsd-kernel` to `freebsd-kernel-core`. Remote kernel "
"debugging is still handled by the `gdb-remote` plugin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:351
msgid ""
"Support for libfbsdvmcore has been removed. As a result, FreeBSD kernel dump "
"debugging is now only available on FreeBSD hosts. Live kernel debugging "
"through the GDB remote protocol is still available from any platform."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:354
msgid "Support for ARM, PPC64le, and RISCV64 has been added."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:355
msgid "The crashed thread is now automatically selected on start."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:356
msgid "Threads are listed in incrmental order by pid then by tid."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:357
msgid ""
"Unread kernel messages saved in `msgbufp` are now printed when LLDB starts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:358
msgid ""
"Writing to the core is now supported. For safety reasons, this feature is "
"off by default. To enable it, `plugin.process.freebsd-kernel-core.read-only` "
"must be set to `false`. This setting is available when using `/dev/mem` or a "
"kernel dump. However, since `kvm_write()` does not support writing to kernel "
"dumps, writes to a kernel dump will still fail when the setting is false."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:362
msgid ""
"Added a command `process plugin refresh-threads`, enabling on-demand thread-"
"list reconstruction from `/dev/mem` so users can resync live kernel thread "
"state without restarting LLDB. Note that this has no impact on full dump and "
"minidump files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:366
msgid "Linux"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:368
msgid ""
"On Arm Linux, the `tpidruro` register can now be read. Writing to this "
"register is not supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:369
msgid ""
"Thread local variables are now supported on Arm and RISC-V Linux if the "
"program being debugged is using glibc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:370
msgid ""
"LLDB now supports AArch64 Linux systems that only have SME (as opposed to "
"SVE and SME). See the AArch64 Linux [documentation](https://lldb.llvm.org/"
"use/aarch64-linux.html#sme-only-systems) for more details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:374
msgid ""
"Prior to this version of LLDB, there was a bug that caused LLDB to crash on "
"startup on these systems ([#138717](https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/"
"issues/138717)). This affected LLDB versions from 18 up to and including 22. "
"17 and below are not affected. If you are using such a system and cannot "
"change LLDB version, or want to package an affected version in a way that is "
"compatible with these systems, the issue contains details of backports that "
"could be done to fix the affected versions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:380
msgid ""
"When an ELF core file is loaded, LLDB now shows the command line that "
"created the core file. If you need to see it again, use the command `process "
"status -v`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:382
msgid ""
"LLDB now supports debugging Linux [Memory Protection Keys](https://docs."
"kernel.org/core-api/protection-keys.html) on AArch64 systems that have the "
"Permission Overlay Extension (POE / FEAT_S1POE). See the [LLDB on AArch64 "
"Linux](https://lldb.llvm.org/use/aarch64-linux.html#permission-overlay-"
"extension-poe) guide for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:387
msgid "Windows"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:389
msgid ""
"Python 3.11 or later is now recommended for building LLDB 23 on Windows. "
"From LLDB 24, Python 3.11 or later will be required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:390
msgid ""
"Messages from `OutputDebugString[A|W]` are now shown inline when using LLDB "
"from the command-line and in the output window when using lldb-dap."
msgstr ""

